#. macro: <if ($n4 == 16)><if ($n1 < $n2)>Mine <noun-en Item 3 $n5 2 1> near Cenote Neyozzote<else>Deliver <noun-en Item 2 $n5 2 1> to Kageel Ja</if><else><if ($n4 == 17)… — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = number parameter 4 == 16 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
